# Everything here is excluded from the build context -- the tarball Docker ships
# to the daemon before the first instruction runs. Two reasons this matters:
#
#   1. Size. A large context makes every build slow, even cached ones.
#   2. Security. Anything sent can end up in a layer. `.git` in particular
#      carries full history, including credentials that were "removed" in a
#      later commit but remain in earlier ones.

.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
tests
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
